      <!-- H2 2: Understanding Whitespace Normalization -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          Understanding Whitespace Normalization: How Unwanted Spaces Corrupt Text
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Extra whitespace is one of the most persistent formatting nuisances in digital publishing, computer programming, and academic writing. It frequently originates from:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>PDF Copy-Pasting:</strong> Portable Document Format (PDF) files store characters at physical coordinate positions rather than semantic word structures. Copying text from a multi-column PDF often inserts double spaces, erratic line breaks, and stray tabs.</li>
          <li><strong>OCR Scans &amp; Automated Transcriptions:</strong> Optical Character Recognition (OCR) tools often misinterpret column gutters and paper margins as strings of consecutive spaces.</li>
          <li><strong>Disjointed Word Processors:</strong> Merging content between Microsoft Word, Google Docs, Slack, and email clients often results in mixed indentation styles, invisible non-breaking spaces, and trailing line whitespace.</li>
          <li><strong>Code Indentation Mismatches:</strong> Mixing tab characters with spaces can introduce compiler warnings in languages like Python or disrupt layout alignment across IDEs.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- H2 3: Regex-Powered Text Cleaning -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          High-Speed Regex-Powered Text Cleaning in the Browser
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          FastToolVerse applies optimized, non-blocking regular expressions designed to process large text files smoothly without hanging your browser thread:
        </p>
        <div class="not-prose my-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 font-mono text-xs text-purple-300 overflow-x-auto space-y-2">
          <div><span class="text-slate-500">// 1. Collapse multiple consecutive horizontal spaces into one</span></div>
          <div>text = text.replace(/[^\S\r\n]+/g, ' ');</div>
          <div class="pt-2"><span class="text-slate-500">// 2. Convert tabs to 4 standard spaces</span></div>
          <div>text = text.replace(/\t/g, '    ');</div>
          <div class="pt-2"><span class="text-slate-500">// 3. Trim leading and trailing spaces per line</span></div>
          <div>text = text.split('\n').map(line => line.trim()).join('\n');</div>
          <div class="pt-2"><span class="text-slate-500">// 4. Remove completely blank lines</span></div>
          <div>text = text.split('\n').filter(line => line.trim() !== '').join('\n');</div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          By operating selectively on horizontal whitespace while respecting standard line returns (<code class="text-xs font-mono bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">\n</code>), FastToolVerse guarantees that your paragraphs retain their intended semantic structure while all visual clutter is eliminated.
